| Phase                         | What you're doing                                  | Typical tools                             |
| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| **1. Scope & Rules**          | Determine what you're authorized to test           | Rules of engagement                       |
| **2. Reconnaissance**         | Gather information about the target                | `whois`, Google, DNS tools                |
| **3. Enumeration**            | Discover ports, services, users, directories, etc. | `nmap`, `ffuf`, `gobuster`, `feroxbuster` |
| **4. Vulnerability Analysis** | Determine what weaknesses may exist                | Nmap scripts, Burp Suite, manual analysis |
| **5. Exploitation**           | Safely exploit a discovered weakness               | Burp, Metasploit, custom scripts          |
| **6. Initial Access**         | Obtain a foothold                                  | Shell, web session, credentials           |
| **7. Post-Exploitation**      | Determine what access you've gained                | Linux/Windows commands                    |
| **8. Privilege Escalation**   | Move from low privilege to higher privilege        | `sudo`, SUID, services, permissions       |
| **9. Lateral Movement**       | Move between systems/accounts when authorized      | Credentials, SSH, SMB, etc.               |
| **10. Objectives / Impact**   | Demonstrate what the vulnerability allows          | Proof of access/data                      |
| **11. Cleanup**               | Remove test artifacts and restore changes          | Logs/files/accounts as permitted          |
| **12. Reporting**             | Document findings and remediation                  | Report, evidence, recommendations         |

# Note:
It's one thing to be able to have the space to download, the ability to download as well as the resources to use tools,
but it's another thing to know how the tools work. By understanding how tools were built and work you are able to use the tool
more easily and with better results.

